        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Staying cool on a treadmill is mostly about air: move it, cool it
            and dry it.</strong> A fan raised to chest height and aimed at your torso does more than
            anything else, and a cooler, drier room does the rest.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Wear less, keep water within reach, run the hard sessions at the coolest time of day, and
            judge effort rather than pace when it is warm. Stop for dizziness, nausea or a
            headache, and call 911 for confusion or fainting. For the fan we would buy and the
